{
  "_comment": [
    "World frame for the composed ORBIT scene: metres, Y-up, right-handed.",
    "The background GLB is already metric and defines the frame, so it is placed at identity;",
    "every human sequence is native millimetre and is scaled by 0.001.",
    "",
    "The stage faces +Z (backdrop wall sits at -Z, lighting truss and access stairs at +Z),",
    "so performers on the deck face yaw~0 and the audience on the ground faces yaw~180.",
    "",
    "yaw_deg is the WORLD direction the subject should face, measured from +Z, turning toward +X.",
    "native_facing_deg is the direction the subject faces in its OWN raw coordinates, same",
    "convention. The composer rotates each subject by (yaw_deg - native_facing_deg).",
    "native_facing_deg values were read off rendered orbit sheets, not computed - these subjects",
    "turn while they move, so they are a best-fit starting orientation, not an exact quantity.",
    "",
    "anchor_* come from scripts/calibrate_sequences.py: floor_y_mm is the 10th percentile of",
    "per-frame min-Y over the sequence (its contact-with-floor level) and center_x/z_mm is the",
    "mean horizontal bbox centre over the sequence. Subtracting the anchor puts the subject's",
    "feet at the origin while preserving its motion relative to that anchor."
  ],
  "world_units": "meters",
  "mm_to_world": 0.001,
  "background": {
